        "id": "comment_tutorial",
        "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
        "data": {
          "comment": "# 📝 Prompt Template\n\nThe pattern behind most NodeTool workflows: typed inputs fill a reusable prompt, an LLM answers it, and the output renders. This one explains a topic for any audience.\n\n**How it works:** \"1️⃣ Topic\" and \"2️⃣ Audience\" are typed string inputs. \"3️⃣ Fill template\" places them into `{{ topic }}` and `{{ audience }}` in a fixed set of instructions that asks for four parts in under 200 words. This separates what varies from what stays fixed. \"4️⃣ Ask the LLM\" is an Agent with no tools, so it makes one plain LLM call. \"Explanation\" exposes the answer to the app UI. Pick a language model on \"4️⃣ Ask the LLM\" before running.\n\n**Try this:** Rewrite the prompt in \"3️⃣ Fill template\" to ask for a recipe that uses `{{ topic }}` as the main ingredient. The graph does not have to change."
        },
        "ui_properties": {
